error[dli::syntax::stray-option]: an `option` belongs to a `question` or a `fork` — none is open above it.
  --> line 1:1
  |
1 | option lonely
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ no question here
  |
  = what: an `option` stands here with no `question` or `fork` open above it, so it is an arm of no choice
  = fix:  put it under a `question q-nnnn "…"` (or a `fork`) on the line above
  = rule: an option is one arm of an undecided fork; without its question there is no debt for it to belong to, and a dangling option is a choice about nothing  (koan 5 — an open question is a debt; 01-syntax.md §3)
